However, a TPSA of 50,000 Å² is physically impossible for a small molecule with 13 heavy atoms and a molecular weight of 178.18 Da. Based on its chemical structure (*p*-propionylbenzoic acid contains one carboxylic acid group contributing 37.30 Å² and one ketone carbonyl oxygen contributing 17.07 Å²), the true TPSA is **54.4 Å²** (54.37 Å²), which is **not** greater than 61.2 Å² (**no**).

{"answer": "no", "concerns": ["The tool reported a TPSA of 50000 square angstroms for CID 20202 (p-Propionylbenzoic acid), which is an extreme, physically impossible outlier for a small molecule of molecular weight 178.18 Da and 13 heavy atoms; the true TPSA of p-propionylbenzoic acid is 54.4 square angstroms."]}

